# Refactor Analytics: Split Monolithic Endpoint into Granular `groupBy` Queries

Refactor the single `GET /api/v1/links/:shortCode/analytics` endpoint (which executes all analytics queries in parallel and returns one large payload) into a query-parameter-dispatched design where the `groupBy` param selects which analytics dimension to fetch. The frontend will issue independent requests per dimension, enabling progressive rendering.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Backend — Schema Validation

#### [NEW] [analytics.schema.ts](file:///d:/Workspace/URLShortener/server/app/schemas/analytics.schema.ts)

Create `analyticsQuerySchema` (Zod) that validates:

| Field | Source | Validation | Default |
|---|---|---|---|
| `shortCode` | `params` | alphanumeric, 1–15 chars (reuses existing regex from `shortCodeSchema`) | — |
| `groupBy` | `query` | enum: `timeseries \| referrers \| countries \| devices \| top_links` (required) | — |
| `start` | `query` | ISO 8601 datetime string | 30 days ago |
| `end` | `query` | ISO 8601 datetime string | now |
| `timezone` | `query` | IANA timezone string | `UTC` |

Defaults for `start`/`end` use `z.string().datetime().optional().default(...)` with computed defaults via `.transform()`. Timezone uses a regex-based check for `Continent/City` format.

