### Backend — Repository Layer

#### [MODIFY] [analytics.repo.ts](file:///d:/Workspace/URLShortener/server/app/repositories/analytics.repo.ts)

**Replace** the current functions with date-range-filtered, timezone-aware equivalents:

| New function | SQL approach | Key changes |
|---|---|---|
| `getTimeseriesRepo(shortCode, start, end, timezone)` | Raw SQL: `DATE(clicked_at AT TIME ZONE $tz) AS date` with `GROUP BY`, `ORDER BY date ASC` | Adds `start/end` filter + timezone conversion (currently hardcoded to 30 days, no TZ) |
| `getReferrersRepo(shortCode, start, end)` | Prisma `groupBy` on `referrer` with date filter | Adds `start/end` filter (currently no date filter) |
| `getCountriesRepo(shortCode, start, end)` | Raw SQL `GROUP BY country` with date filter | **Extracted** from the CTE query — becomes standalone |
| `getDevicesRepo(shortCode, start, end)` | Raw SQL CTE for `device_type`, `browser`, `os` with date filter | **Extracted** from the CTE query — country removed from CTE |
| `getTopLinksRepo(userId, start, end)` | Raw SQL: join `url_mappings` → `click_logs`, `GROUP BY short_code`, `ORDER BY clicks DESC LIMIT 10` | **New** — no existing equivalent |

**Preserved functions** (unchanged):
- `isLinkOwnedByUserRepo` — still needed by controller
- `getClickLogsRepo` — used by the separate `/clicks` endpoint

All new functions use parameterized queries (Prisma tagged templates or Prisma `where` clauses). No string interpolation.

