### Frontend — React Query Hook

#### [MODIFY] [useLinkAnalyticsData.ts](file:///d:/Workspace/URLShortener/frontend/src/hooks/useLinkAnalyticsData.ts)

Replace the single `useQuery(['linkAnalytics', shortCode])` with **four independent** `useQuery` calls:

| Query key | API function | Enabled when |
|---|---|---|
| `['linkAnalytics', shortCode, 'timeseries']` | `getLinkAnalyticsTimeseries` | `!!shortCode && isPlanLoaded && isVip` |
| `['linkAnalytics', shortCode, 'referrers']` | `getLinkAnalyticsReferrers` | same |
| `['linkAnalytics', shortCode, 'countries']` | `getLinkAnalyticsCountries` | same |
| `['linkAnalytics', shortCode, 'devices']` | `getLinkAnalyticsDevices` | same |

Each query independently handles `PLAN_REQUIRED` errors. The hook returns:

```typescript
{
  link: LinkItem | null;
  timeseries: TimeseriesItem[] | null;
  referrers: ReferrerItem[] | null;
  countries: BreakdownItem[] | null;
  devices: DeviceBreakdown | null;
  isPlanGated: boolean;
  isLoading: boolean;   // true only while link query is loading
  error: string | null;
}
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> `isLoading` now only tracks the **link info** query. Individual analytics cards manage their own loading state via the query status passed through props or separate loading checks.

